---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Write-through on direct-mapped-8, timed 1/20: a store miss stalls for the fill, a store hit costs the hit time alone although it writes memory too, and a load that evicts a clean line stalls for the fill only (cases 8, 6 and 3)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 0 | Store 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, cycles | 1 | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | 1 | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | stall | timing | - | 1 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while memory supplies line 0x0A0.
1.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills, cycles | 21 | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.6 | write | writePolicy | word 2/0/1 | 21 | Write 7 into word 1 of way 0.
1.7 | writeThrough | writePolicy | memory 0xA4, writethroughs | 21 | Write-through: 7 also goes to memory at 0x0A4.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 21 | Store 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
2.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits, cycles | 22 | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
2.3 | write | writePolicy | word 2/0/2 | 22 | Write 9 into word 2 of way 0.
2.4 | writeThrough | writePolicy | memory 0xA8, writethroughs | 22 | Write-through: 9 also goes to memory at 0x0A8.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 22 | Load 0x1A4: tag 0x03, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, cycles | 23 | Set 2 holds tag 0x01, not 0x03. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | 23 | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
3.4 | stall | timing | - | 23 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while memory supplies line 0x1A0.
3.5 | evict | associativity | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | 23 | Evict line 0x0A0 (tag 0x01) from way 0.
3.6 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills, cycles | 43 | Fill way 0 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
3.7 | complete | - | r1 | 43 | Read word 1 of way 0 (12) into r1.
